        /// @brief Tear down the LB grid at batch end — delete every child
        ///        Memory and reset the root's grid links.
        ///
        /// @details
        /// Each LB's four `HashMemory` instances ride the LB's cold arena
        /// (`overallHashMemory` / `localHashMemory` / `localHashMemoryDelta` /
        /// `workingMemory`, all on `lbMemory.manager`) but are declared BEFORE
        /// that arena, so at member destruction their `encodedMap`'s
        /// `~PagedVector` would run AFTER the arena and `freePage` on freed
        /// storage. This empties every LB's `encodedMap` while its arena is
        /// alive — each child before its `delete`, the root in place — so
        /// destruction is harmless. The root's remaining containers live inside
        /// `lbMemory` (declared after its arena) and already destruct in the safe
        /// order. Run after the proof-graph export, the grid's last reader, so
        /// nothing reads the LBs afterward.
        ///
        /// @invariant On return `simpleMapStore` is empty and `permanentBodies`
        ///            holds only the root.
        /// @see `generateRawProofGraph` (the export run immediately before).
        void destroyGrid();

